465	          <p class="ds-alert-title">Destructive buttons always require a confirmation step</p>
466	          <p>A dialog, an inline confirm/cancel reveal, or at minimum a clear undo path. Never fire a destructive action on single click without giving the user a chance to reconsider. The button colour signals danger; the UX pattern must back that signal up.</p>
