666	      <p class="callout">
667	        <strong>Accessibility checklist:</strong> (1) <code>aria-label</code> on every icon button — no exceptions. (2) <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> on the icon element or SVG so screen readers don't announce raw glyph names. (3) For custom SVGs, also add <code>focusable="false"</code> to prevent IE/Edge from making the SVG itself focusable.
668	      </p>
669	      <p class="callout">
670	        <strong>Toggle / Pressed state (<code>aria-pressed</code>):</strong> Use <code>aria-pressed="true"</code> on icon buttons that represent persistent on/off state — e.g., a filter toggle, a grid/list view switcher, or a "show deleted" control. Set <code>aria-pressed="false"</code> when off (restores default appearance). The filled icon glyph (<code>bi-funnel-fill</code> vs <code>bi-funnel</code>) provides an additional visual signal alongside the pressed style. Constructive and Destructive variants represent single-fire actions (edit, delete) and should not use <code>aria-pressed</code>.
671	      </p>
